IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa24-officers`
IMPORT `coa24-penalty`
IMPORT `coa24-identity`

-- coa24-acsp.l4: Part 35 "Authorised corporate service providers", ss 1098A to 1098H of the Companies Act 2006
-- (lines 15677-15775 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ANSWERS FOR THE OTHER PARTS. The Act's index (Schedule 8) says "authorised corporate service provider"
-- is defined by s 1098A: `s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider`.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT ENCODED. ss 1098B(6)-(7), 1098C(5)-(6), 1098F(2)-(5), 1098G(1)-(4), (6)-(7) and 1098H(1), (3)-(4) are powers
-- of the Secretary of State to make regulations: machinery, inert (reason 2) in NOTES.md. The Money Laundering
-- Regulations 2017 are not among the sources: whether a person is "a relevant person" under regulation 8(1), what
-- regulation 7 makes a supervisory authority, and the requirements any regulations add are facts or inputs here.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A function whose name ends "meets the requirement of s N" answers JUST FALSE when the
-- "must" it cites is not done: that is a fork line in NOTES.md, not a ruling.

§ `Part 35: authorised corporate service providers (ss 1098A to 1098H)`

-- ---- s 1098A ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15679 | In this Act “authorised corporate service provider” means a person—
-- src:15680 | (a) whose application to the registrar to become an authorised corporate service provider for the purposes of this Act has been granted (see section 1098B),
-- src:15681 | (b) who has not since ceased to be an authorised corporate service provider by virtue of section 1098F, and
-- src:15682 | (c) whose status as an authorised corporate service provider is not for the time being suspended by virtue of section 1098F.
@ref s 1098A Meaning of "authorised corporate service provider" (src:15679-15682)
GIVEN `the person's application to the registrar to become an authorised corporate service provider has been granted (see section 1098B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has since ceased to be an authorised corporate service provider by virtue of section 1098F` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's status as an authorised corporate service provider is for the time being suspended by virtue of section 1098F` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider` MEANS
    IF `the person's application to the registrar to become an authorised corporate service provider has been granted (see section 1098B)` AND (NOT `the person has since ceased to be an authorised corporate service provider by virtue of section 1098F`) AND (NOT `the person's status as an authorised corporate service provider is for the time being suspended by virtue of section 1098F`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Act “authorised corporate service provider” means a person— (a) whose application to the registrar ... has been granted ..., (b) who has not since ceased ... and (c) whose status ... is not for the time being suspended"

-- ---- s 1098B ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15684 | (1) A person may apply to the registrar to become an authorised corporate service provider for the purposes of this Act if—
-- src:15685 | (a) the person is a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations,
-- src:15686 | (b) in the case of an individual, their identity is verified (see section 1110A), and
-- src:15687 | (c) the person meets any other requirements imposed by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 1098B(1) Who may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider (src:15684-15687)
GIVEN `the person is a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person meets any other requirements imposed by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of paragraph (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may apply to the registrar to become an authorised corporate service provider for the purposes of this Act if— (a) the person is a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations"
    ELSE CONSIDER (IF `the person is an individual` THEN `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` ELSE JUST TRUE)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in the case of an individual, their identity is verified (see section 1110A)"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER `the person meets any other requirements imposed by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of paragraph (c)`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) the person meets any other requirements imposed by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph"
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the requirements imposed by regulations under paragraph (c) are not in the sources
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the individual's identity is verified is answered by section 1110A and was not supplied

-- src:15688 | (2) An application under this section must contain—
-- src:15689 | (a) the name of the applicant’s supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations,
-- src:15690 | (b) the required information about the applicant (see section 1098C), and
-- src:15691 | (c) in the case of an application by an individual, a statement that the individual’s identity is verified (see section 1110A).
-- src:15692 | (See also section 1098D, which imposes restrictions on who may deliver an application under this section on behalf of a firm.)
@ref s 1098B(2) What an application must contain (src:15688-15692)
GIVEN `the application contains the name of the applicant's supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains the required information about the applicant (see section 1098C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a statement that the individual's identity is verified (see section 1110A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098B(2) the application meets the requirement of s 1098B(2)` MEANS
    IF       `the application contains the name of the applicant's supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations`
         AND `the application contains the required information about the applicant (see section 1098C)`
         AND ((NOT `the applicant is an individual`) OR `the application contains a statement that the individual's identity is verified (see section 1110A)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under this section must contain— (a) the name of the applicant’s supervisory authority or authorities ..., (b) the required information about the applicant (see section 1098C), and (c) in the case of an application by an individual, a statement that the individual’s identity is verified"

-- src:15693 | (3) Where an application is made under this section, the registrar must check with the supervisory authority, or at least one of the supervisory authorities, specified in the application, to find out whether the applicant is known to and supervised by that authority.
@ref s 1098B(3) The registrar must check with the supervisory authority (src:15693)
GIVEN `an application is made under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098B(3) the registrar must check with the supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `an application is made under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an application is made under this section"

-- src:15699 | (5) The registrar must refuse the application if it appears to the registrar that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry out the functions of an authorised corporate service provider.
@ref s 1098B(5) The registrar must refuse the application if the applicant is not a fit and proper person (src:15699)
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry out the functions of an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098B(5) the registrar must refuse the application` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the registrar that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry out the functions of an authorised corporate service provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must refuse the application if it appears to the registrar that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry out the functions of an authorised corporate service provider"

-- src:15694 | (4) Having carried out that check, the registrar must grant the application if—
-- src:15695 | (a) the supervisory authority, or at least one of the supervisory authorities, specified in the application has confirmed that the applicant is known to and supervised by that authority,
-- src:15696 | (b) where the applicant is an individual, the registrar is satisfied that their identity is verified (see section 1110A),
-- src:15697 | (c) any other conditions that may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph are met, and
-- src:15698 | (d) the registrar is not required by subsection (5) to refuse the application.
@ref s 1098B(4) The registrar must grant the application if the four conditions are met (src:15694-15698)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority, or at least one of the supervisory authorities, specified in the application has confirmed that the applicant is known to and supervised by that authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar is satisfied that the applicant's identity is verified (see section 1110A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other conditions specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of paragraph (c) are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the registrar that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry out the functions of an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the supervisory authority, or at least one of the supervisory authorities, specified in the application has confirmed that the applicant is known to and supervised by that authority`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar must grant the application if— (a) the supervisory authority, or at least one of the supervisory authorities, specified in the application has confirmed that the applicant is known to and supervised by that authority"
    ELSE IF `the applicant is an individual` AND (NOT `the registrar is satisfied that the applicant's identity is verified (see section 1110A)`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the applicant is an individual, the registrar is satisfied that their identity is verified (see section 1110A)"
         ELSE IF `s 1098B(5) the registrar must refuse the application` `it appears to the registrar that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry out the functions of an authorised corporate service provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) the registrar is not required by subsection (5) to refuse the application"
              ELSE CONSIDER `any other conditions specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of paragraph (c) are met`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) any other conditions that may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph are met"
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the conditions specified by regulations under paragraph (c) are not in the sources

-- src:15702 | (8) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:15703 | “Money Laundering Regulations” means the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692);
-- src:15704 | “supervised”: a person is supervised by a supervisory authority if regulation 7(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations provides that it is a supervisory authority for that person;
-- src:15705 | “supervisory authority” means an authority that is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations (see regulation 7 of those Regulations).
@ref s 1098B(8) "Money Laundering Regulations", "supervised" and "supervisory authority" (src:15702-15705)
`s 1098B(8) the Money Laundering Regulations` MEANS "the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692)"

@ref s 1098B(8) "supervised" (src:15704)
GIVEN `regulation 7(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations provides that the authority is a supervisory authority for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098B(8) the person is supervised by the supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `regulation 7(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations provides that the authority is a supervisory authority for the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“supervised”: a person is supervised by a supervisory authority if regulation 7(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations provides that it is a supervisory authority for that person"

@ref s 1098B(8) "supervisory authority" (src:15705)
GIVEN `the authority is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations (regulation 7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098B(8) the authority is a supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `the authority is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations (regulation 7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“supervisory authority” means an authority that is a supervisory authority under the Money Laundering Regulations"

-- ---- s 1098C ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each field says the particular is supplied, or (for (ea) and (f)) that there is none to supply.
DECLARE `s 1098C(1) particulars supplied for a firm` HAS
    `s 1098C(1)(a) firm name` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(1)(b) principal office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(1)(c) a service address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(1)(d) an email address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(1)(e) the legal form of the firm and the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(1)(ea) any registration number allocated to the firm under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(1)(f) if applicable, any other register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:15707 | (1) The “required information” about the applicant, in the case of a firm that is applying to become an authorised corporate service provider, means—
-- src:15708 | (a) firm name,
-- src:15709 | (b) principal office,
-- src:15710 | (c) a service address,
-- src:15711 | (d) an email address,
-- src:15712 | (e) the legal form of the firm and the law by which it is governed, ...
-- src:15713 | (ea) any registration number allocated to the firm in respect of its registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations, and
-- src:15714 | (f) if applicable, any other register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register.
@ref s 1098C(1) The required information about a firm (src:15707-15714)
GIVEN particulars IS A `s 1098C(1) particulars supplied for a firm`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098C(1) the application contains the required information about the firm` MEANS
    IF       particulars's `s 1098C(1)(a) firm name`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(1)(b) principal office`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(1)(c) a service address`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(1)(d) an email address`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(1)(e) the legal form of the firm and the law by which it is governed`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(1)(ea) any registration number allocated to the firm under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(1)(f) if applicable, any other register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “required information” about the applicant, in the case of a firm that is applying to become an authorised corporate service provider, means— (a) firm name, (b) principal office, (c) a service address, (d) an email address, (e) the legal form of the firm and the law by which it is governed"

-- s 1098C(3) and (4): "name" means forename and surname; a peer or an individual usually known by a title may give the title instead.
-- src:15721 | (3) In subsection (2)(a) “name” means forename and surname.
-- src:15722 | (4) Where the applicant is a peer or an individual usually known by a title, the requirement for the application to contain their name may be satisfied by providing that title instead of the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 1098C(3), (4) "name" (src:15721-15722)
GIVEN `a forename and surname are supplied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a peer or an individual usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the title is supplied instead of a forename and surname` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098C(3) the name supplied meets the requirement to contain the applicant's name` MEANS
    IF `a forename and surname are supplied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the applicant is a peer or an individual usually known by a title` AND `the title is supplied instead of a forename and surname`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In subsection (2)(a) “name” means forename and surname"

DECLARE `s 1098C(2) particulars supplied for an individual` HAS
    `s 1098C(2)(a) nationality` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(2)(a) date of birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(2)(b) a service address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(2)(c) an email address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(2)(d) the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is usually resident or, if usually resident outside the United Kingdom, that country or state` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1098C(2)(e) any registration number allocated to the individual under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:15715 | (2) The “required information” about the applicant, in the case of an individual who is applying to become an authorised corporate service provider, means—
-- src:15716 | (a) name, nationality and date of birth,
-- src:15717 | (b) a service address,
-- src:15718 | (c) an email address, ...
-- src:15719 | (d) the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is usually resident or, if the person is usually resident in a country or state outside the United Kingdom, that country or state , and
-- src:15720 | (e) any registration number allocated to the individual in respect of their registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations.
@ref s 1098C(2) The required information about an individual (src:15715-15720)
GIVEN `the name requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      particulars IS A `s 1098C(2) particulars supplied for an individual`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098C(2) the application contains the required information about the individual` MEANS
    IF       `the name requirement is met`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(2)(a) nationality`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(2)(a) date of birth`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(2)(b) a service address`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(2)(c) an email address`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(2)(d) the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is usually resident or, if usually resident outside the United Kingdom, that country or state`
         AND particulars's `s 1098C(2)(e) any registration number allocated to the individual under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “required information” about the applicant, in the case of an individual who is applying to become an authorised corporate service provider, means— (a) name, nationality and date of birth, (b) a service address, (c) an email address"

-- src:15723 | (4A) For the purposes of this section “Money Laundering Regulations” has the meaning given by section 1098B(8) (application to become authorised corporate service provider).
@ref s 1098C(4A) "Money Laundering Regulations" has the meaning given by s 1098B(8) (src:15723)
`s 1098C(4A) the meaning of "Money Laundering Regulations"` MEANS `s 1098B(8) the Money Laundering Regulations`

-- ---- s 1098D ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1098D firm` IS ONE OF
    `s 1098D a company`
    `s 1098D a body corporate other than a company`
    `s 1098D a limited partnership`
    `s 1098D a partnership other than a limited partnership`
    `s 1098D an unincorporated body other than a partnership`

DECLARE `s 1098D position of the individual` IS ONE OF
    `s 1098D a director`
    `s 1098D a member of the body`
    `s 1098D an officer of the body whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company`
    `s 1098D a general partner as defined by section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907`
    `s 1098D a member of the partnership`
    `s 1098D a member of the governing body`
    `s 1098D another position`

-- src:15729 | An application under section 1098B by a firm mentioned in the first column of the table—
-- src:15730 | (a) must be delivered to the registrar on its behalf by a relevant officer mentioned in the second column who is an individual (see also section 1067A(2)), and
-- src:15731 | (b) must be accompanied by a statement by the individual confirming their status as a relevant officer of the firm.
-- src:15732 | Firm | Relevant officer
-- src:15733 | company | director
-- src:15734 | body corporate other than a company | where the body’s affairs are managed by its members, a member of the body;in any other case, any officer of the body whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company.
-- src:15735 | partnership | in relation to a limited partnership, a general partner as defined by section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907;in relation to any other partnership, a member of the partnership
-- src:15736 | unincorporated body other than a partnership | where the body’s affairs are managed by its members, a member of the body;in any other case, a member of the governing body.
@ref s 1098D The firms and their relevant officers (the table) (src:15729-15736)
GIVEN firm IS A `s 1098D firm`
      `the body's affairs are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 1098D position of the individual`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` MEANS
    CONSIDER firm
    WHEN `s 1098D a company` THEN
        IF position EQUALS `s 1098D a director`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant officer mentioned in the second column" (company | director)
    WHEN `s 1098D a body corporate other than a company` THEN
        IF `the body's affairs are managed by its members`
        THEN IF position EQUALS `s 1098D a member of the body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant officer mentioned in the second column" (where the body's affairs are managed by its members, a member of the body)
        ELSE IF position EQUALS `s 1098D an officer of the body whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant officer mentioned in the second column" (in any other case, any officer of the body whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company)
    WHEN `s 1098D a limited partnership` THEN
        IF position EQUALS `s 1098D a general partner as defined by section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant officer mentioned in the second column" (in relation to a limited partnership, a general partner as defined by section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907)
    WHEN `s 1098D a partnership other than a limited partnership` THEN
        IF position EQUALS `s 1098D a member of the partnership`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant officer mentioned in the second column" (in relation to any other partnership, a member of the partnership)
    WHEN `s 1098D an unincorporated body other than a partnership` THEN
        IF `the body's affairs are managed by its members`
        THEN IF position EQUALS `s 1098D a member of the body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant officer mentioned in the second column" (where the body's affairs are managed by its members, a member of the body)
        ELSE IF position EQUALS `s 1098D a member of the governing body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant officer mentioned in the second column" (in any other case, a member of the governing body)

@ref s 1098D(a), (b) The application must be delivered by a relevant officer who is an individual, with a statement of status (src:15729-15731)
GIVEN firm IS A `s 1098D firm`
      `the body's affairs are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 1098D position of the individual`
      `the person who delivers the application on the firm's behalf is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by a statement by the individual confirming their status as a relevant officer of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098D the application meets the delivery requirements of s 1098D` MEANS
    IF `the person who delivers the application on the firm's behalf is an individual` AND (`s 1098D table the position is a relevant officer of the firm` firm `the body's affairs are managed by its members` position EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the application is accompanied by a statement by the individual confirming their status as a relevant officer of the firm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under section 1098B by a firm mentioned in the first column of the table— (a) must be delivered to the registrar on its behalf by a relevant officer mentioned in the second column who is an individual ..., and (b) must be accompanied by a statement by the individual confirming their status as a relevant officer of the firm"

-- ---- s 1098E ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) "within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the change occurs": the day of the change is the
-- first of the 14, so the last day is 13 days after it.
-- src:15738 | (1) A person who is an authorised corporate service provider must notify the registrar of any change in its supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the change occurs.
-- src:15739 | (2) Where the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations, for the purposes of this section the change is not to be treated as having occurred until the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3).
@ref s 1098E(1)-(2) Notifying the registrar of a change in supervisory authority (src:15738-15739)
GIVEN `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the change occurs` IS A DATE
      `date on which the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1098E(1)-(2) the last day for notifying the registrar of the change` MEANS
    IF `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations`
    THEN CONSIDER `date on which the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3)`
         WHEN JUST notified THEN JUST (notified PLUS 13)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the change is not treated as having occurred until the authority notifies or publishes, and it has not yet done so
    ELSE JUST (`date on which the change occurs` PLUS 13)

-- (2): "the change is not to be treated as having occurred until the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person
-- or publishes the agreement": an "until" bar. Before the date it is JUST TRUE that the change cannot yet be treated as
-- having occurred; from that date it is JUST FALSE.
@ref s 1098E(2) The change is not treated as having occurred until the authority notifies or publishes (src:15739)
GIVEN `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `date on which the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098E(2) the change cannot yet be treated as having occurred` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations"
    ELSE CONSIDER `date on which the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3)`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST notified THEN
             IF `date on which the question is asked` LESS THAN notified
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the change is not to be treated as having occurred until the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement" (it has)

-- src:15740 | (3) A person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with this section commits an offence.
@ref s 1098E(3) A person who without reasonable excuse fails to comply with this section commits an offence (src:15740)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not notified the registrar of the change within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has no reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098E(3) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is an authorised corporate service provider` AND `the person has not notified the registrar of the change within the period` AND `the person has no reasonable excuse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with this section commits an offence"

-- The same duty, with the dates worked out: the person notified the registrar on a date (or has not), and the day the
-- question is asked is known.
-- src:15738 | (1) A person who is an authorised corporate service provider must notify the registrar of any change in its supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the change occurs.
-- src:15739 | (2) Where the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations, for the purposes of this section the change is not to be treated as having occurred until the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3).
-- src:15740 | (3) A person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with this section commits an offence.
@ref s 1098E(1)-(3) Whether the person has failed to notify the registrar within the period (src:15738-15740)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the change occurs` IS A DATE
      `date on which the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the person notified the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the person has no reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1098E(1)-(2) the last day for notifying the registrar of the change` `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations` `date on which the change occurs` `date on which the authority that has agreed to act notifies the person or publishes the agreement under regulation 7(3)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the change is not yet treated as having occurred, so no period is running
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        CONSIDER `date on which the person notified the registrar`
        WHEN JUST notified THEN
            `s 1098E(3) the person commits an offence` `the person is an authorised corporate service provider` (notified GREATER THAN lastDay) `the person has no reasonable excuse`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            `s 1098E(3) the person commits an offence` `the person is an authorised corporate service provider` (`date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN lastDay) `the person has no reasonable excuse`

-- src:15741 | (4) Where the offence is committed by a firm, every officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence.
@ref s 1098E(4) Every officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence (src:15741)
GIVEN `the offence was committed by` IS A `Kind of person`
      `s 1098E(3) the offence was committed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person`
      conduct IS A `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098E(4) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `the offence was committed by`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1098E(3) the offence was committed`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 1121 the person is an officer in default` position conduct
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the offence is committed by a firm" and the offence of subsection (3) is not made out on the facts given
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the offence is committed by a firm"

-- src:15742 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:15743 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:15744 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1098E(5) The punishment on summary conviction (src:15742-15744)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHEN Scotland THEN Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- src:15745 | (6) In this section “Money Laundering Regulations” and “supervisory authority” have the meanings given by section 1098B(8).
@ref s 1098E(6) "Money Laundering Regulations" and "supervisory authority" (src:15745)
`s 1098E(6) the section that gives the meaning of "Money Laundering Regulations" and "supervisory authority"` MEANS "section 1098B(8)"

-- The duty of subsection (1) as a regulative rule. The trace clock counts days from the day the change occurs (day 0);
-- the last timely day is day 13.
DECLARE `s 1098E(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1098E(1) the authorised corporate service provider`
    `s 1098E(1) the registrar`

DECLARE `s 1098E(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1098E(1) notify the registrar of the change in supervisory authority`

-- src:15738 | (1) A person who is an authorised corporate service provider must notify the registrar of any change in its supervisory authority or authorities for the purposes of the Money Laundering Regulations within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the change occurs.
@ref s 1098E(1) A person who is an authorised corporate service provider must notify the registrar within 14 days (src:15738)
`s 1098E(1) the provider's duty to notify the registrar of the change` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1098E(1) the authorised corporate service provider`
    MUST `s 1098E(1) notify the registrar of the change in supervisory authority`
    WITHIN 13
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1098E(1) the authorised corporate service provider` BECAUSE "the registrar was not notified of the change in supervisory authority within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the change occurred"

-- ---- s 1098F ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15747 | (1) A person ceases to be an authorised corporate service provider if the person ceases to be a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations.
@ref s 1098F(1) A person ceases to be an authorised corporate service provider on ceasing to be a relevant person (src:15747)
GIVEN `the person ceases to be a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098F(1) the person ceases to be an authorised corporate service provider` MEANS
    IF `the person ceases to be a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (2) lets regulations provide other circumstances in which a person ceases, and the "if" of subsection (1) does not close them

-- src:15757 | (6) In this section “Money Laundering Regulations” has the meaning given by section 1098B(8).
@ref s 1098F(6) "Money Laundering Regulations" (src:15757)
`s 1098F(6) the section that gives the meaning of "Money Laundering Regulations"` MEANS "section 1098B(8)"

