-- src:15770 | (2) In subsection (1) “relevant regulatory regime” means a regulatory regime that, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, has similar objectives to the regulatory regime under the Money Laundering Regulations for relevant persons and is likely to be no less effective in achieving those objectives.
@ref s 1098H(2) "relevant regulatory regime" (src:15770)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the regime has similar objectives to the regulatory regime under the Money Laundering Regulations for relevant persons and is likely to be no less effective in achieving those objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
